(# A problem statement is `problem.tex` followed by `problem-extra.tex` if there is one --
   appended directly, with no heading of its own, because the extra is a continuation of the
   statement rather than a section beside it.

   Shared by `blocks/problem.jtex` (booklet, tearoffs) and by `standalone.jtex` (the
   one-problem preview), so the preview cannot drift from the real thing. #)
\protectedInput{\activeDirectory/(* language.id *)/problem.tex}%
\IfFileExists{\activeDirectory/(* language.id *)/problem-extra.tex}{%
    \protectedInput{\activeDirectory/(* language.id *)/problem-extra.tex}%
}{}%
